        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Research Question:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Methodology:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;2. Retrieval Methods and Approaches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;The basis of measurement stands on the soil dielectric properties which depend on the volumetric SMC parameter. For completeness, there is a significant difference between the dielectric properties of water (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;ε&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;≈ 80) and the dry soil (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;ε&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;≈ 4) [&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(79, 86, 113);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/12/4/614?utm_source=chatgpt.com#B1-remotesensing-12-00614&quot; title=&quot;&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;]. Assuming this dependency, SMC can be estimated by determining the dielectric constant (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;ε&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;) to which the radar backscattering coefficient intensity (σ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;) is related by measuring through active sensors (radars), and to the emissivity (E) by passive sensors (radiometers).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Main Findings:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vegetation Effects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Limitations:&lt;/p&gt;
