        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_68"/>
        <dc:title>SoilMoistureMapper: a GNSS-R approach for soil moisture retrieval on UAV</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Measuring of distribution of the soil moisture (SM) content is an essential requirement in precision agriculture. This paper demonstrates practical and low-cost soil moisture mapping techniques based on Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) Reflectometry (GNSS-R) observations via a small-size unmanned-aerial vehicle (UAV). An SM estimation model is developed using a random forest (RF) machinelearning (ML) algorithm combining GNSS-R signals with ancillary vegetation indices from a multispectral camera. The ML model is trained and tested using in-situ data from eight SM probes located in a 2.48ha farm. The study results showed that SM maps of the field can be obtained with about 13 mins flight with 5m × 5m spatial resolution. The developed ML model reached RMSE of 0.032m3m−3 and R-value of 0.93 in 10-fold cross-validation.




The study results showed that SM maps of the field can be obtained with about 13 mins flight with 5m × 5m spatial resolution</dcterms:abstract>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>Zotero</z:libraryCatalog>
    </bib:Article>
